Actually, what really makes most sense is "9 times less likely."
Essentially, the question "how much less likely" means "how much more
infrequently?" (I.e. wraiths fail to leave corpses at a given rate on
most levels; how much does that failure rate go up on a graveyard
level?) Since the failure rate (infrequency) goes up by nine times
(for every time a wraith fails to leave a corpse on a normal level, it
does so nine times on a graveyard level) the question "how much less
likely" should be answered by "nine times less likely." (As pointed
out earlier, "1/9 as likely" means the same thing.) "1/9 less likely"
would actually mean that wraith corpses appear on graveyard levels
nine times more than they do on normal levels!

